      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "When a polynomial in $x$ is graphed, the exponents will always be integers, the leading coefficient (the first coefficient in standard form) will always be the coefficient of the term with highest exponent, and the variable term (or the one with the variable exponent $x$) will always be in front of the constant term.\nFrom this picture $f(x)=\\frac{1}{8}x(x-1)(x-2)$, so $a=\\frac{1}{8}$, $b=-\\frac{1}{2}$, $c=1$, and $d = 0$.  Then $8a-4b+2c-d=4\\left(\\frac{1}{8}\\right)+2\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)+2=1-1+2=\\boxed{2}$. The answer is: 2",
