      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the value of \\(8a - 4b + 2c - d\\), we need to use the information given by the graph. The graph of the function \\(f(x) = ax^3 + bx^2 + cx + d\\) is a cubic polynomial that passes through the following points based on the behavior of the curve:\n\n- It has roots at \\(x = -1\\), \\(x = 0\\), and \\(x = 3\\).\n- It crosses the x-axis at these points, meaning \\(f(-1) = 0\\), \\(f(0) = 0\\), and \\(f(3) = 0\\).\n\nFirst, let's use the fact that \\(f(0) = 0\\):\n\\[ f(0) = d = 0. \\]\nSince \\(d = 0\\), the function simplifies to:\n\\[ f(x) = ax^3 + bx^2 + cx. \\]\n\nNext, let's use the fact that \\(f(-1) = 0\\):\n\\[ f(-1) = a(-1)^3 + b(-1)^2 + c(-1) = -a + b - c = 0. \\]\nThis gives us the equation:\n\\[ -a + b - c = 0. \\]\nRearranging terms, we get:\n\\[ b - c = a. \\quad \\text{(Equation 1)} \\]\n\nNow, let's use the fact that \\(f(3) = 0\\):\n\\[ f(3) = a(3)^3 + b(3)^2 + c(3) = 27a + 9b + 3c = 0. \\]\nThis gives us the equation:\n\\[ 27a + 9b + 3c = 0. \\]\nWe can divide the entire equation by 3 to simplify:\n\\[ 9a + 3b + c = 0. \\quad \\text{(Equation 2)} \\]\n\nWe now have a system of linear equations:\n1. \\( b - c = a \\)\n2. \\( 9a + 3b + c = 0 \\)\n\nWe can solve this system by eliminating \\(c\\). From Equation 1, we can express \\(c\\) in terms of \\(a\\) and \\(b\\):\n\\[ c = b - a. \\]\nSubstitute \\(c = b - a\\) into Equation 2:\n\\[ 9a + 3b + (b - a) = 0. \\]\nSimplify the equation:\n\\[ 9a + 3b + b - a = 0, \\]\n\\[ 8a + 4b = 0, \\]\n\\[ 2a + b = 0, \\]\n\\[ b = -2a. \\]\n\nNow substitute \\(b = -2a\\) back into \\(c = b - a\\):\n\\[ c = -2a - a, \\]\n\\[ c = -3a. \\]\n\nSo, we have \\(b = -2a\\) and \\(c = -3a\\). We need to find the value of \\(8a - 4b + 2c - d\\). Since \\(d = 0\\) and \\(c = -3a\\), we substitute these values into the expression:\n\\[ 8a - 4b + 2c - d = 8a - 4(-2a) + 2(-3a) - 0, \\]\n\\[ 8a + 8a - 6a = 10a. \\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\(8a - 4b + 2c - d\\) is \\(\\boxed{0}\\).",
