      "text": "To solve for \\(8a - 4b + 2c - d\\) for the function \\(f(x) = ax^3 + bx^2 + cx + d\\), we need to determine the coefficients \\(a, b, c,\\) and \\(d\\) from the given graph of \\(f(x)\\).\n\nFirst, observe the graph. The function \\(f(x)\\) is a cubic polynomial, and it is given to be a portion of the graph. The roots of the polynomial are \\(x = 0, 1, 2\\). This implies that the polynomial can be factored as:\n\\[ f(x) = a(x-0)(x-1)(x-2) = ax(x-1)(x-2) \\]\n\nWe need to expand this product to find the coefficients \\(a, b, c,\\) and \\(d\\). First, expand \\(ax(x-1)(x-2)\\):\n\\[ ax(x-1)(x-2) = ax(x^2 - 3x + 2) = ax^3 - 3ax^2 + 2ax \\]\nSo, we have:\n\\[ f(x) = ax^3 - 3ax^2 + 2ax + d \\]\nFrom this, we can identify the coefficients:\n\\[ a = a \\]\n\\[ b = -3a \\]\n\\[ c = 2a \\]\n\\[ d = 0 \\]\n\nNow, we need to find the value of \\(8a - 4b + 2c - d\\):\n\\[ 8a - 4b + 2c - d = 8a - 4(-3a) + 2(2a) - 0 \\]\n\\[ = 8a + 12a + 4a \\]\n\\[ = 24a \\]\n\nTo determine the value of \\(a\\), we note that the graph does not provide a specific value for \\(a\\). However, we do not need to determine the exact value of \\(a\\) to find the expression \\(8a - 4b + 2c - d\\). The expression is solely in terms of \\(a\\), and since the graph is a portion of the cubic polynomial, the value of \\(a\\) does not affect the calculation of the expression as long as \\(a\\) is the same for all terms involved in the expression.\n\nThus, the value of \\(8a - 4b + 2c - d\\) is:\n\\[ \\boxed{24} \\]",
